### Session 01 · Raw LLM call — run this in Visual Studio 2022 (.http files) or VS Code "REST Client"
### Put your key in an environment variable called GROQ_API_KEY first.

@baseUrl = https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
@key = {{$processEnv GROQ_API_KEY}}

### 1. Simple chat completion
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile",
  "messages": [
    { "role": "system", "content": "You are a witty senior .NET developer. Keep answers under 40 words." },
    { "role": "user", "content": "Explain what an LLM is to a C# developer." }
  ],
  "temperature": 0.7
}

### 2. List the models your key can use
GET {{baseUrl}}/models
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}

### 3. Streaming (watch the data: lines arrive)
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "llama-3.1-8b-instant",
  "stream": true,
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "Count from 1 to 10 in words." } ]
}
